# Changing the key the session authenticated with ends that session and
# answers a plain status with no CMAC. The old key then fails and the new key
# authenticates; GetKeyVersion reports the new version under EV1 secure
# messaging.
#
# Generated from tests/test_dfc_virtual_picc_mutation_vectors.c
# (/aes-change-key-same-key-round-trip) by recording the exchanges the
# reference engine performed, then cross-checked: all 10 byte
# expectations asserted by that test matched the recording exactly.
# 4 further exchanges carry no byte expectation in the source.
#
# The ChangeKey cryptograms are computed at runtime by the original test
# from the derived session key, so they are recorded rather than
# transcribed. inject-random pins RndB ahead of every authentication so
# the vector does not depend on the engine's default generator.
#
# The two assert steps are the credential-state checks the original makes on
# credential.apps[0] straight after the ChangeKey.

name: AES ChangeKey on the authenticated key
case-id: mutation-aes-change-key-same-key
origin: synthetic
requires: auth-aes
